;;; A flat import of a library of facts brings none of its facts — M1f
;;; **W88**, register row `W88/import-facts-flat`
;;; (`corpus/wrong_answers.toml`), filed by S1f.6.11 (T1f.6.11.2, 2026-11-11)
;;; on the user's ruling of that day, *"importing facts is mandatory"*.
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; `import-facts-library.ein`, beside this file, is an ontology: it declares
;;; `is-a` and states `(is-a Tea Drink)` and `(is-a Milk Drink)`. This program
;;; imports `is-a` from it flat, states nothing of its own, and asks what is a
;;; drink. No candidate, so R is {∅}.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; A listed name selects the module's declaration of it and every top-level
;;; fact whose relation it is (S1f.6.11's point (a)), so root holds the
;;; library's two `is-a` facts, as it would had they been written here, and
;;; the goal has two rows: *Tea is a drink* and *Milk is a drink*. The
;;; library's `likes` facts and its rule `liquids` are not listed and nothing
;;; kept names them, so they stay behind.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ───────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `7f574423`, release: the program loads with the declaration and no
;;; fact, in silence, and the read-out says *the goal has no row: undetermined
;;; here*, exit 0, on every command that answers a goal; `ein saturate --dump`
;;; lists no `is-a` fact. `(import import-facts-library :as o)` kept the two
;;; facts, renamed `(o.is-a …)`.
;;; The answer above by hand since S1f.6.11 (T1f.6.11.3).

(import import-facts-library :symbols (is-a))

(solve :hypothesis-relations ())
(query :goal (is-a ?x Drink) :goal-text "{?x} is a drink")
